// People drawn as lines (language spec §7.1): a stroke across the lane at birth, the name, a line to the
// death date and a stroke across the lane there. A life still going, or running past either end of the
// timeline, gets a torn edge instead of the stroke. Spans and groups stay as bars, for contrast.
timeline start=1840 end=2026 length=60cm width=200 baseline=low

// Born before the timeline starts: a torn edge at the start instead of a birth stroke
^!!person "Charles Darwin" 1809-1882 green
^!person "Charles Babbage" 1791-1871 blue
^person "Isambard Kingdom Brunel" 1806-1859 grey

^!!person "Florence Nightingale" 1820-1910 red
^!person "Louis Pasteur" 1822-1895 indigo
^person "James Clerk Maxwell" 1831-1879 blue
^person "Thomas Edison" 1847-1931 orange
^person "Nikola Tesla" 1856-1943 violet
^!!person "Marie Curie" 1867-1934 red
^!person "Albert Einstein" 1879-1955 blue
^person "Emmy Noether" 1882-1935 green
^person "Grace Hopper" 1906-1992 indigo
^!person "Alan Turing" 1912-1954 black
^person "Katherine Johnson" 1918-2020 orange
^person "Richard Feynman" 1918-1988 violet
^person "Rosalind Franklin" 1920-1958 red
^person "Peter Higgs" 1929-2024 grey
^person "Stephen Hawking" 1942-2018 blue

// Still alive: a torn edge at the timeline's end
^!person "David Attenborough" 1926- green
^person "Tim Berners-Lee" 1955- indigo

// Labels too long for the life: beside it, or pulled out with a leader from the line
^person "Yuri Gagarin, the first person in space" 1934-1968 red
^person "Henry Moseley" 1887-1915 grey
^person "Emily Brontë" 1818-1848 violet
^person "Frank Ramsey, philosopher and economist" 1903-1930 green
vperson "Anne Frank, diarist of the Secret Annex" 1929-1945 orange

// Events crossing people's lines: each pole has a short gap where it crosses a line
^event "On the Origin of Species" 1859-11-24
^!event "Apollo 11 lands" 1969-07-20 time_label=day
^event "The World Wide Web" 1991-08-06

// Spans below, still drawn as bars
v!!span "First World War" 1914-1918 black fill=diagonal
v!!span "Second World War" 1939-1945 black fill=diagonal
v!span "Cold War" 1947-1991 grey
